WEBVTT

00:03.940 --> 00:06.400
I won't fall for you.

00:06.400 --> 00:07.770
You're just a Pig's Foot.

00:20.060 --> 00:23.580
Makabe Masamune at his 
absolute best yet again today.

00:24.070 --> 00:27.700
I am truly like the rising sun!

00:27.700 --> 00:30.950
Yikes, guess you're still full of yourself.

00:31.730 --> 00:32.340
Gah!

00:32.340 --> 00:36.030
Chinatsu! I thought I told you 
not to just barge in here!

00:36.030 --> 00:38.510
Yeah, whatever. Man, you're loud.

00:38.510 --> 00:40.600
Control yourself when you're in France.

00:40.600 --> 00:42.200
Don't embarrass all of Japan.

00:40.600 --> 00:42.600
<b>Class Trip  France</b>

00:40.600 --> 00:42.600
<b>Yasaka High School</b>

00:43.480 --> 00:45.960
Good morning, Maa-kun and Chinatsu-chan!

00:45.960 --> 00:47.100
It's time for breakfast.

00:47.470 --> 00:49.040
You're leaving today, aren't you?

00:49.040 --> 00:51.610
I went all-out for you today!

00:51.610 --> 00:54.860
There's fried chicken, 
fried shrimp, and even gratin!

00:52.530 --> 00:54.860
<b>High in calories</b>

00:53.030 --> 00:54.860
<b>High in calories</b>

00:53.780 --> 00:54.860
<b>High in calories</b>

00:55.320 --> 00:57.370
Yay, gratin!

00:57.370 --> 00:59.580
Maa-kun, is there anything 
else you'd like to ea—

00:59.580 --> 01:01.930
Both of you, out!

01:02.800 --> 01:04.590
Damn that loli hag...

01:04.590 --> 01:07.980
How could I eat something so high 
in calories first thing in the morning?

01:10.360 --> 01:13.550
<i>The greatest opportunity since the 
cultural festival has presented itself!</i>

01:13.550 --> 01:16.430
<i>The City of Flowers is truly a perfect 
place to exact my revenge.</i>

01:16.430 --> 01:20.790
<i>And that's when I'll get a checkmate 
in my Dead or Love plan!</i>

01:27.570 --> 01:30.570
Are you ready, Aki-sama?

01:30.570 --> 01:31.570
Yes.

01:32.040 --> 01:34.970
Could you take my suitcase, Yoshino?

01:34.970 --> 01:36.570
As you wish.

01:46.120 --> 01:48.440
Get me a gift, 'kay thanks.

01:48.440 --> 01:51.750
Maa-kun, come home soon, okay?

01:51.750 --> 01:52.910
Maa-kun!

01:52.910 --> 01:55.640
Yeah, yeah. I'll see you later.

03:27.010 --> 03:32.980
<b>#1 "The Wee Parisian Mademoiselle"</b>

03:33.870 --> 03:38.350
<i>Dearest Muriel, I saw the piece you sent me.</i>

03:38.350 --> 03:40.510
<i>It's quite a masterpiece.</i>

03:40.510 --> 03:42.110
<i>One piece of advice I have for you:</i>

03:42.110 --> 03:46.120
<i>you should learn more about 
Japanese high school students.</i>

03:46.120 --> 03:48.370
So it <i>is</i> hopeless.

03:48.370 --> 03:50.500
No matter how much I practice...

03:54.620 --> 03:56.730
High school students from Japon...

03:58.200 --> 03:59.830
They're just too far away.

04:00.260 --> 04:02.220
Wow...

04:02.560 --> 04:07.950
An art museum was made in the 
Louvre Palace during the French Revolution.

04:07.950 --> 04:10.640
It can easily be called the 
greatest art museum in the world.

04:10.640 --> 04:14.350
<b></b>Traveling Through France

04:11.030 --> 04:13.960
Sans crème s'il vous plait...

04:14.670 --> 04:17.720
"Without whipped cream, please."

04:17.720 --> 04:21.500
<i>I've never seen Kojuurou 
study so hard in his life.</i>

04:21.500 --> 04:23.310
What should I do, Makabe-kun?

04:23.310 --> 04:26.080
We're in the land of macarons, 
canelés, and bon bon chocolats!

04:26.080 --> 04:27.610
Can you believe it?!

04:27.610 --> 04:29.790
Try to calm down a bit, Kojuurou.

04:29.790 --> 04:32.450
Fashion! The Opera House! Ballet!

04:32.450 --> 04:36.920
Love and romance! Amore!

04:36.920 --> 04:38.200
What you're trying to say is...

04:38.200 --> 04:41.320
What you're trying to say 
is "amour," Futaba-san.

04:41.320 --> 04:43.550
"Amore" is Italian.

04:58.260 --> 05:00.490
<i>So you've come, Cruel Princess.</i>

05:00.490 --> 05:03.860
Aki-chan, there was a 
churros shop over there.

05:04.170 --> 05:06.110
<i>And there's the bumpkin fiancé.</i>

05:06.490 --> 05:08.500
<i>There he goes, getting in my way again.</i>

05:12.180 --> 05:14.480
<i>No, no. Calm down.</i>

05:14.480 --> 05:16.710
<i>For me, this class trip should be—</i>

05:23.210 --> 05:27.510
<i>We're definitely in the land of amour! 
PDA everywhere!</i>

05:28.770 --> 05:31.600
<i>This country is truly the best place for this.</i>

05:32.470 --> 05:38.460
<i>I'm going to make Adagaki Aki fall for me, 
and then dump her on the spot.</i>

05:38.460 --> 05:41.570
<i>So that I can move my 
Dead or Love plan forward!</i>

05:42.090 --> 05:44.190
Just you wait, Cruel Princess!

05:44.190 --> 05:46.030
The rising sun...

05:46.030 --> 05:49.300
No, Soleil le Vant!

05:49.300 --> 05:50.010
Hey.

05:50.010 --> 05:50.990
Huh?

05:51.310 --> 05:54.860
Could you keep some time open 
during our free periods on this trip?

05:54.860 --> 05:57.370
What's that supposed to mean?

05:57.370 --> 05:59.080
Exactly what it sounds like.

05:59.390 --> 06:02.170
I've been thinking ever 
since the cultural festival

06:02.170 --> 06:06.050
that I should actually take some 
time to properly talk to you.

06:06.050 --> 06:09.710
<i>Th-This is... Wait, what the heck's going on?</i>

06:09.710 --> 06:14.010
Anyway, this is a promise! 
I'll make you pay if you break it!

06:14.010 --> 06:16.330
U-Uh, w-wait—

06:19.690 --> 06:22.220
O-Oh, no! A French girl?

06:22.220 --> 06:23.210
Hey!

06:23.210 --> 06:24.570
H-How do I apologize?

06:24.570 --> 06:25.940
<b></b>Schedule Book

06:24.570 --> 06:25.940
<b></b>Translation

06:27.490 --> 06:29.100
Excusez moi!

06:31.170 --> 06:32.700
Ca nefaitrien.

06:32.970 --> 06:33.960
<i>An eyepatch?</i>

06:34.530 --> 06:37.440
Are you Japonais?

06:37.440 --> 06:38.810
Did she just speak Japanese?

06:39.570 --> 06:43.100
Y-Yes, I'm Japanese. I'm in high school.

06:44.270 --> 06:46.040
A high school student...

06:46.040 --> 06:47.880
Japanese...

06:50.420 --> 06:54.970
Yes! You're the one I was 
looking for, my Chikuwa-kun!

06:58.760 --> 07:01.650
My name is Muriel Besson!

07:02.200 --> 07:04.410
I am a second-year in high school.

07:04.410 --> 07:06.280
I'm Makabe Masamune.

07:06.740 --> 07:08.330
I'm Adagaki Aki.

07:08.330 --> 07:11.580
Your Japanese is very good. 
Did you study it somewhere?

07:11.580 --> 07:16.320
Why, yes! I learned a lot from 
anime and manga from Japon, I did!

07:16.320 --> 07:17.910
Manga, eh?

07:18.300 --> 07:21.120
Manga from Japon is fantastic!

07:21.120 --> 07:26.630
Every time my brother goes to Tokyo for work, 
I ask him to buy me lots of manga!

07:26.940 --> 07:28.450
<i>She's...</i>

07:28.450 --> 07:30.090
<i>...definitely an otaku.</i>

07:30.090 --> 07:34.720
I hope that one day I'll be able 
to draw manga like that, I do.

07:34.720 --> 07:36.250
Wait, you?

07:37.720 --> 07:42.720
Well, we do have bande dessinée in France.

07:42.720 --> 07:46.570
But what I want to draw is 
Japonais manga, it is!

07:50.520 --> 07:51.930
You drew this?

07:51.930 --> 07:55.110
Yes! I still have much to work on, but...

07:55.820 --> 07:57.580
<b>Leave it to Tsumire</b>

08:05.800 --> 08:12.300
I want to draw a poppy and exciting rom-com 
about Tsumire-san, who lives in Tokyo!

08:12.300 --> 08:13.280
Rom-com?!

08:13.280 --> 08:17.370
Why in the world are the names of the 
heroine and hero Tsumire and Chikuwa?

08:17.370 --> 08:20.770
Because my favorite Japanese food is oden!

08:23.400 --> 08:27.200
Does something seem off to you?

08:27.200 --> 08:29.160
I'm not sure if "off" is the right word...

08:29.160 --> 08:31.990
I do have a lot of questions...

08:32.470 --> 08:34.670
My older brother also told me

08:34.670 --> 08:38.970
that I should learn more about 
Japanese high school students.

08:39.760 --> 08:43.460
When I first saw you, I thought Chikuwa-kun 
was standing right in front of me!

08:43.460 --> 08:44.390
Huh?

08:44.990 --> 08:47.920
You're the ideal Japanese 
high school boy, Masamune.

08:48.240 --> 08:51.560
Please let me use you 
as a model for my manga!

08:51.560 --> 08:52.000
What?!

08:52.000 --> 08:52.810
What?

08:52.810 --> 08:56.400
What do real high school boys think about?

08:56.400 --> 08:59.640
Do you prefer toast for breakfast? 
Or perhaps sushi?

08:59.640 --> 09:00.760
Um...

09:00.760 --> 09:01.850
Yes?

09:02.360 --> 09:05.440
I'm flattered that you're so interested,

09:05.440 --> 09:07.690
but I'm currently on vacation...

09:08.800 --> 09:11.480
Is there any way you'd consider it?

09:14.260 --> 09:16.200
What do I do?

09:16.200 --> 09:20.660
Hey, are you saying you don't care 
about your promise with me?

09:22.160 --> 09:23.770
I'm sorry, Muriel-san.

09:23.770 --> 09:26.860
We're but humble high school 
students on their class trip.

09:26.860 --> 09:29.130
Humble?

09:29.130 --> 09:31.780
Oh, you mean like the samurai?

09:31.780 --> 09:32.870
No.

09:33.200 --> 09:38.780
A-Anyway, we have to stay with our class, 
so we don't have much free time,

09:38.780 --> 09:43.300
and when I do, I plan to go around with her.

09:44.580 --> 09:46.460
Hey! What's the big idea?

09:46.460 --> 09:48.520
Throw me a bone here!

09:49.240 --> 09:52.720
So, even though I'd like to help 
you out, I just don't have time.

09:52.720 --> 09:53.980
I'm really sorry.

09:55.280 --> 09:57.290
I see...

09:57.780 --> 10:00.720
I cannot force you, I cannot.

10:00.720 --> 10:03.220
I'll be rooting for you. Good luck.

10:19.020 --> 10:22.300
Fujinomiya-san, do you like that painting?

10:22.300 --> 10:24.840
Yes, though I'm not sure if 
"like" is the right word.

10:24.840 --> 10:27.260
I just feel uneasy looking at it.

10:28.510 --> 10:32.250
Look, they're not wearing anything on top.

10:32.250 --> 10:33.790
Oh, right.

10:33.790 --> 10:37.860
Feeling cold can lead to many ailments. 
I want to lend them something to wear.

10:38.140 --> 10:41.190
<i>Fujinomiya-san's so nice...</i>

10:42.010 --> 10:43.900
Oh, yeah, Fujinomiya-san!

10:43.900 --> 10:44.680
Yes?

10:45.080 --> 10:48.680
Um, um, um...

10:50.400 --> 10:52.990
You're looking quite pale 
yourself, Kojuurou-san.

10:52.990 --> 10:55.560
No! I'm totally fine.

10:56.150 --> 10:57.130
Oh?

11:02.980 --> 11:04.990
What's the matter, you two?!

11:04.990 --> 11:06.940
Can someone get us some stretchers?

11:07.360 --> 11:09.660
Mind your own business, Commando.

11:10.620 --> 11:13.150
I don't want to excite them any more.

11:13.150 --> 11:14.730
"Them"?

11:15.340 --> 11:17.120
We're safe here, aren't we?

11:17.120 --> 11:19.950
Yeah, it looks like it.

11:24.720 --> 11:27.270
I thought I was going to die...

11:28.840 --> 11:30.910
She sure was strange.

11:31.410 --> 11:33.900
I'll say that she's definitely passionate.

11:36.400 --> 11:39.080
Anyway, get off of me already!

11:39.080 --> 11:40.280
Whoa...

11:42.630 --> 11:44.310
S-Sorry...

11:45.300 --> 11:46.410
Makabe.

11:53.300 --> 11:54.190
Venez.

12:03.130 --> 12:06.460
Adagaki-san, is your French decent?

12:06.460 --> 12:08.360
I can basically say, "Can I get the check,"

12:08.360 --> 12:11.040
and "Is there anyone who understands Japanese?"

12:11.040 --> 12:13.130
Good. We're on the same level.

12:13.130 --> 12:16.010
Why are you relieved 
right now?! Are you stupid?

12:18.070 --> 12:20.030
M-Marcy bocut!

12:20.030 --> 12:21.070
Crowassant!

12:21.070 --> 12:22.220
Escargoo!

12:22.220 --> 12:24.970
Arch of Triumph! Huh?

12:25.600 --> 12:29.930
<i>It's a pleasure to meet you, 3D Chikuwa-kun.</i>

12:30.400 --> 12:32.840
My name is Frank Besson.

12:32.840 --> 12:37.150
I'm the older brother of the 
girl you just rejected, Muriel.

12:37.560 --> 12:41.980
My position is the reverse of yours right now. 
I'm actually in Tokyo on business.

12:41.980 --> 12:44.330
Japan sure is a nice place.

12:45.400 --> 12:48.040
<i>B-Business, you say?</i>

12:48.660 --> 12:52.870
No matter. That's not the 
issue here. It's what you did.

12:53.130 --> 12:55.530
<i>Why did you decline Muriel's request?</i>

12:55.530 --> 12:57.210
Huh? Uh...

12:57.210 --> 13:01.660
<i>The worst sin you can commit 
in this world is making Muriel cry.</i>

13:01.660 --> 13:05.840
<i>The second-worst sin you can commit 
in this world is disappointing Muriel!</i>

13:07.550 --> 13:10.300
If you want to stay with that girl there,

13:10.300 --> 13:14.970
how about you two teach Muriel 
the essence of a rom-com?

13:14.970 --> 13:18.040
That's simple enough, isn't it, Chikuwa-kun?

13:22.130 --> 13:25.640
Ah... So when you get a day with free time,

13:25.640 --> 13:29.800
you have to spend it with Aki-sama 
and this otaku mademoiselle.

13:30.640 --> 13:33.200
Can I ask how that happened?

13:33.200 --> 13:35.350
I honestly have no idea.

13:38.200 --> 13:44.110
I'm sorry. Everything was ruined despite 
you setting it all up for me, Master.

13:44.110 --> 13:46.130
Me? What did I do?

13:47.090 --> 13:48.760
You didn't?

13:48.760 --> 13:51.890
I figured the Cruel Princess 
wouldn't invite me to talk to her

13:52.170 --> 13:54.170
one-on-one without your help...

13:56.900 --> 13:58.350
Seriously?

13:58.830 --> 14:02.620
Wait, does that mean she invited me herself?

14:03.190 --> 14:05.030
I'm honestly surprised myself.

14:05.570 --> 14:10.030
I should actually take some 
time to properly talk to you.

14:10.300 --> 14:12.310
<i>She looked pretty serious...</i>

14:13.170 --> 14:16.810
But it's a good thing that 
Aki-sama seems proactive.

14:16.810 --> 14:18.750
R-Right...

14:18.750 --> 14:23.150
I'll help you out so that 
no one else gets in your way.

14:23.150 --> 14:24.220
Thanks.

14:31.400 --> 14:34.780
Oh, sorry. Kojuurou and the 
others are waiting for me.

14:41.250 --> 14:42.380
Master.

14:44.440 --> 14:46.190
I'm seriously counting on you.

14:56.830 --> 15:00.540
How long are you gonna be in 
the shower? Get out already, Gasou.

15:00.540 --> 15:03.880
Sorry. Just hang on a little longer.

15:04.520 --> 15:08.550
<i>Jeez, I can't even get changed 
in peace. How annoying.</i>

15:09.270 --> 15:12.800
Aki-chan, there was a churros shop over there.

15:12.800 --> 15:15.000
Why don't we go there together?

15:15.000 --> 15:17.370
Sorry, I've got something to do.

15:19.160 --> 15:20.980
<i>Makabe Masamune.</i>

15:20.980 --> 15:23.100
<i>You accursed man.</i>

15:23.100 --> 15:25.600
<i>I need money, damn it...</i>

15:25.600 --> 15:29.230
<i>So that I can preserve the Gasou name and status.</i>

15:29.230 --> 15:31.630
<i>Love and gender don't matter.</i>

15:31.630 --> 15:33.500
<i>Money is everything.</i>

15:34.820 --> 15:37.160
<i>I catch a red snapper using a shrimp...</i>

15:37.830 --> 15:40.540
<i>Nay, I'll catch money using love.</i>

15:40.960 --> 15:45.000
<i>I call this brilliant plan... "Fishing."</i>

15:49.640 --> 15:52.260
<i>I guess neither of us got any sleep.</i>

15:52.670 --> 15:55.450
Okay, let's go, Adagaki-san.

15:55.450 --> 15:56.720
Right...

15:57.180 --> 15:59.200
Are you really okay?

15:59.200 --> 16:01.820
Weren't you threatened 
by some really scary people?

16:01.820 --> 16:04.040
Want us to tag along quietly?

16:04.040 --> 16:06.440
I think we'll be fine...

16:06.800 --> 16:12.010
We're counting on you if we don't 
make it back in time, Commando.

16:20.520 --> 16:22.430
Masamune! Aki!

16:22.430 --> 16:24.970
You actually came, you did!

16:24.970 --> 16:29.070
I was so excited for today that 
I was tingling with excitement!

16:29.070 --> 16:31.000
Do you mean "trembling with excitement"?

16:31.000 --> 16:31.720
Oui!

16:34.360 --> 16:37.100
<i>She's so serious about this...</i>

16:37.580 --> 16:39.000
<i>Ah, well...</i>

16:41.190 --> 16:43.440
Okay, let's begin.

16:43.440 --> 16:45.080
First, Besson-san...

16:45.080 --> 16:47.260
You can call me Muriel.

16:47.260 --> 16:48.960
Okay, Muriel.

16:48.960 --> 16:51.360
There's something I want to 
ask you about this manga.

16:51.360 --> 16:52.900
Really?

16:54.600 --> 16:56.610
First, this right here.

16:56.970 --> 17:00.700
He asked her out three panels ago, 
and they're totally a thing now.

17:01.320 --> 17:03.420
Is there a problem with that?

17:04.830 --> 17:09.260
As someone who's read all the volumes of 
the monumental classic of romance manga,

17:09.260 --> 17:11.300
"<i>Rose-eyed Steroid</i>," let me say...

17:11.300 --> 17:13.120
When it comes to rom-coms...

17:13.120 --> 17:16.010
Once they both fall for each other, 
80% of the story is over!

17:16.010 --> 17:19.050
Tease! Tease until you can tease no more!

17:19.050 --> 17:20.590
Tease?

17:20.590 --> 17:21.580
Yes.

17:21.580 --> 17:24.480
You can make it all count in the remaining 20%,

17:24.480 --> 17:28.250
but it's a cruel path that 
I cannot recommend to beginners.

17:29.240 --> 17:30.940
I have no idea what you're talking about.

17:30.940 --> 17:32.160
But why?!

17:32.160 --> 17:34.800
I mean, they like each other, right?

17:34.800 --> 17:36.740
Then they should tell each other.

17:38.290 --> 17:41.200
Staring at each other like this

17:42.020 --> 17:44.790
and kissing might also be good.

17:44.790 --> 17:45.660
Hey!

17:45.660 --> 17:47.310
Je t'adore.

17:49.160 --> 17:51.530
Wait, wait, wait!

17:52.770 --> 17:55.310
Unlike French people, normal Japanese people

17:55.310 --> 17:58.840
can't easily tell someone 
else their feelings!

17:58.840 --> 18:01.720
There are times we want to 
be honest, but we can't!

18:01.720 --> 18:04.840
Or something from their past 
might be holding them back.

18:04.840 --> 18:06.330
A lot can happen.

18:06.330 --> 18:08.570
So even if you have feelings for each other,

18:08.570 --> 18:10.570
there's some reason you can't tell them?

18:10.570 --> 18:12.000
Yes, exactly!

18:12.000 --> 18:14.970
Are you talking about you two?

18:17.160 --> 18:20.510
A-A-A-A-A-Are you stupid?!

18:20.510 --> 18:24.320
Aki, your Japanese is hard to understand 
because you speak so fast, it is.

18:24.320 --> 18:26.790
I'm telling you that's inconceivable!

18:28.500 --> 18:29.290
Anyway!

18:29.290 --> 18:32.160
What you need to learn is 
the Japanese form of love.

18:32.160 --> 18:35.070
You are forbidden from becoming 
romantically involved with someone.

18:35.070 --> 18:36.380
Understood?

18:36.380 --> 18:38.510
I understand, I do.

18:38.510 --> 18:42.190
We'll show you how things are done 
as characters in a rom-com,

18:42.190 --> 18:43.740
so make sure you pay attention.

18:43.740 --> 18:44.270
Huh?

18:44.270 --> 18:46.980
Yes! I'm looking forward to this, yes!

18:46.980 --> 18:49.620
Honestly. You're so illogical.

18:50.140 --> 18:52.300
Now, then. To show you how it's done...

18:52.300 --> 18:53.920
How it's done...

18:53.920 --> 18:56.330
How do we do that, exactly?

18:57.040 --> 18:59.950
<i>You didn't think about what to show her, huh?</i>

19:06.160 --> 19:08.620
<i>Japanese romance? I mean...</i>

19:08.960 --> 19:12.330
<i>What should we show her, exactly?</i>

19:14.540 --> 19:16.200
We hit the jackpot!

19:16.200 --> 19:17.950
What do you think, Fujinomiya-san?

19:17.950 --> 19:22.050
I think Masamune-sama might 
enjoy this level of sweetness.

19:23.440 --> 19:25.760
Yeah, you're right.

19:28.130 --> 19:31.950
Fujinomiya-san, do you 
still like Masamune-kun?

19:31.950 --> 19:33.480
Huh? Huh?!

19:34.880 --> 19:37.820
Is that a bit too pathetic 
after he rejected me?

19:37.820 --> 19:40.200
Not at all! Really!

19:41.880 --> 19:45.290
Sometimes, I think about what could've been.

19:45.290 --> 19:47.850
Perhaps if we had met in 
a slightly different way...

19:47.850 --> 19:50.460
Maybe if there wasn't a lie 
involved from the start...

19:51.040 --> 19:54.920
But if I didn't have that lie, 
I would've been too scared to approach him.

19:55.440 --> 19:59.140
I'm sure he's going to suffer 
even more from now on.

19:59.810 --> 20:01.420
Just like me.

20:02.700 --> 20:06.590
I'm sort of looking forward 
to that day, but also not.

20:06.590 --> 20:08.580
It's rather complicated.

20:09.590 --> 20:13.320
I can't really understand complicated things,

20:13.320 --> 20:17.300
b-but since you're so confused 
by this, Fujinomiya-san...

20:19.880 --> 20:22.570
I think you're very profound!

20:24.320 --> 20:27.050
Thank you very much, Kojuurou-san.

20:27.050 --> 20:29.040
What lovely words of encouragement.

20:32.130 --> 20:34.100
<i>I'm such a loser.</i>

20:37.960 --> 20:38.750
Oh?

20:39.560 --> 20:41.290
Is something the matter?

20:41.720 --> 20:43.720
Maybe I'm seeing things...

20:44.240 --> 20:46.220
Yeah, I think I am.

20:50.180 --> 20:53.310
Hey, is this really the right way?

20:53.310 --> 20:57.400
I think we got it right this time. I'm sorry.

20:59.350 --> 21:02.720
Aki-chan wanted to tell me 
something personally, right?

21:02.720 --> 21:04.840
I can't keep her waiting, then.

21:04.840 --> 21:07.510
Sorry. Just a little farther.

21:08.080 --> 21:10.620
<i>Until free time is over...</i>

21:11.750 --> 21:14.580
You just keep apologizing over and over.

21:21.940 --> 21:24.760
Hey. Are you hiding something from me?

21:27.410 --> 21:28.720
I'm sorry.

21:28.720 --> 21:31.520
I was actually lying when I said 
Aki-sama was waiting for you.

21:31.520 --> 21:34.440
What? Why would you lie 
about something like that?

21:35.270 --> 21:40.870
Because... I wanted to spend as much time 
with you as I could, Kanetsugu-sama.

21:42.000 --> 21:45.500
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, Kanetsugu-sama.

21:46.160 --> 21:49.410
O-Oh, jeez...

21:51.440 --> 21:52.980
Yeah, right.

21:53.870 --> 21:57.300
I'm not gonna fall for that anymore,

22:00.480 --> 22:03.250
you betraying little witch.
